Below you will receive task descriptions from which you should generate an Ansible Playbook.  
The generated playbook must be valid inside an Ansible Role under the tasks/ directory (e.g., tasks/main.yml).  
Do not include hosts:, vars:, or any playbook-level headers. Only output valid task entries or blocks as expected in a role.  

Task 1: Import assert.yml
Description Task 1: Import tasks from assert.yml for validation purposes. This task is set to run once on localhost.

Task 2: Install nginx
Description Task 2: Install the nginx package ensuring it is present on the system.

Task 3: Place nginx.conf
Description Task 3: Create and place the nginx configuration file from a template. Includes validation and sets proper file mode.

Task 4: Ensure /etc/nginx/conf.d exists
Description Task 4: Create the conf.d directory for nginx configuration files with proper permissions.

Task 5: Place default.conf
Description Task 5: Create and place the default nginx configuration file from a template. Includes proper file mode and notification for restart.

Task 6: Start and enable nginx
Description Task 6: Start the nginx service and ensure it is enabled to run on boot.


- Last generated (faulty) playbook:
---
- import_tasks: assert.yml
  run_once: true
  delegate_to: localhost

- name: Install nginx
  package:
    name: nginx
    state: present

- name: Place nginx.conf
  template:
    src: nginx.conf.j2
    dest: /etc/nginx/nginx.conf
    validate: /usr/sbin/nginx -t -c %s
    mode: 0644
  notify: restart nginx

- name: Ensure /etc/nginx/conf.d exists
  file:
    path: /etc/nginx/conf.d
    state: directory
    owner: root
    group: root
    mode: 0755

- name: Place default.conf
  template:
    src: default.conf.j2
    dest: /etc/nginx/conf.d/default.conf
    mode: 0644
  notify: restart nginx

- name: Start and enable nginx
  service:
    name: nginx
    state: started
    enabled: true


